Every naltrexone-initiation-opioid-free-interval should last for at least 7 days to 10 days.
If a patient does not provably have a naltrexone-initiation-opioid-free-interval and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not administer a first-naltrexone-dose to the patient.
If a patient has a naltrexone-initiation-opioid-free-interval then every clinician may administer a first-naltrexone-dose to the patient.
